+# On the ROW_MAJOR ring walk cb_output_tiles takes the L1 the solved blocking leaves before the deep im2col ring does (bm
+# is not traded for it), up to a whole M-block: the last K-block's bias pass then waits on the store for fewer row groups,
+# and the writer drains the rest under the next block. Bit-identical. Only where K has at least OUT_DEPTH_FREE_MIN_K_TILES
+# tiles (C_in >= 64): with one-tile taps (C_in 32, 9 tile-MACs per output tile) the store is NoC1 / DRAM bound, and a
+# store that runs on under the next block keeps NoC1 busy without the gaps the last-K-block burst leaves the cores
+# upstream of the DRAM endpoints (grid x 13-15, y 5-10), which then finish last. Measured (Blackhole p150b, FLUX.2
+# bh2x4, device kernel us, 3 runs each, alternating order): 514x1024 64->128 799 -> 779 (17 of 30 row groups),
+# 514x1024 64->256 1373 -> 1358 (6 of 15), the other ring cases flat; 514x1024 32->128 595 -> 605 (+1.5%, median),
+# hence the K floor. A whole-M-block CB paid for with bm measured worse there (1026x2048 32->128 1826 -> 3038,
+# 514x1024 32->128 595 -> 724).
+OUT_DEPTH_FREE = True
+OUT_DEPTH_FREE_MIN_K_TILES = 18
